===Noun===
{{en-noun|p}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} A comparison of items that, however categorically similar, is inapt; an incompatible analogy, or the items so compared; a [[disanalogy]].
#: {{ux|en|It's '''apples and oranges'''. You can't convert square meters to linear inches.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/scotland-blog/2014/jan/17/scotland-police-stopsearch|title=Stop and search in Scotland: record figures need open debate|date=2014-01-17|author=Kath Murray|work=The Guardian|passage=So on the one hand, comparing policing issues in Scotland with what is happening in England may be like comparing '''apples and oranges'''.}}
#* {{quote-hansard|en|date=11 June 2019|url=https://hansard.parliament.uk/Commons/2019-06-11/debates/64948DDA-D25C-4707-8476-F79EBD251B08/SustainableDevelopmentGoals|speaker=Rory Stewart|authorlink=Rory Stewart|house=[[w:House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]]|debate=Sustainable Development Goals|column=592|passage=In comparing Britain with other countries, it is important to remember that we are not comparing like with like; there is an '''apples and oranges''' issue.}}
# {{&lit|en|apples|and|oranges}}

